foreign  [Music]  this is just another one of the half  dozen builds or so that often use in my  story videos where I quite often have  people asking what I'm using so this  will be somewhere quick I can point  people towards  one of the things I love about the  division is that there is a ridiculous  number of options for you to vary up  your builds to completely change the way  you play through content for me I love  playing the sniper from time to time  there's something about the one tap  headshot kill that is incredibly  satisfying  I don't watch build videos and I'll  never claim that whatever I've built is  the best of its type as I'm a strong  believer in the fact that there is no  person on the internet that can throw  some pieces together run the numbers and  decide what is the best most amazing  god-like OP build for your style of play  instead use what you see as a template  and adjust to whatever works best for  you  it's also worth noting that I play solo  the majority of the time so a lot of my  builds are certainly not specked for  group play  I've been playing around and changing  things on this build for the last 12  months and I can absolutely guarantee  that there are many more ways to gain  considerably higher damage numbers but  maybe it's just me but I really don't  like having to proc a dozen different  talents across multiple weapons and  skills in order to get the chance to  land a high damage shot I I just want to  shoot stuff in the head and kill them  with a little hassle but some people  like this so I'll suggest some  alternative pieces along the way  I'm not going to read through the set  perks or each individual Talent  description in order to inflate the  length of this video because by now I'm  sure you know what these are or you can  read for yourself in game  the idea behind this build is  ridiculously straightforward stack all  the headshot damage you can  here I am running four pieces of Aces  and Eights on the mask gloves holster  and knee pads the backpack is the uraldi  Holdings with the Vigilant Talent rolled  onto it eraldi because of the Native  brand seat bonus of 10 maximum rifle  damage the chest is the named Walker  Harris and Co brand set piece called  chain killer which is the perfect  Headhunter Talent  but slightly more damage you could swap  out the knee pads for Sawyers but  personally I move around far too much to  take advantage of this Talent  all pieces have been rolled into weapon  damage for the core attribute and  headshot damage as the secondary  attribute you should be able to get  around 300 or more headshot damage I  spend a lot of time playing around  trying to find a balance between  critical hit chance critical hit damage  and headshot damage to see if I can get  the best of both but I found putting  everything into headshot as being the  most consistent  the primary weapon I use is the white  death for its huge boost to headshot  damage the talent is a lucky shot  because you know I don't have perfect  day you could certainly Swap this out  for something that will increase your  damage further just remember though the  more time you spend reloading the less  damage you'll be doing over time  you may have noticed that I don't run a  maximum scope yes this means I lose out  on up to 45 extra headshot damage but  there is a reason for this  I've enjoyed playing the sniper roll  since the days of the division 1 where I  mainly played on Xbox firstly sniping on  Console at least in the division 1 is  much easier than on PC the auto aim on  controller when popping the left trigger  right trigger over and over was  extremely op hence why I used the lucky  shot Talent on PC  but also the main difference between the  division 1 and 2 is the forced scoping  in division two  it may not be much to most but I find  the scoping far too slow for my  playstyle and also a bit limiting for  the varied range you need to be able to  shoot as a solo player  the secondary weapon is the classic M1A  this is justify I'm struggling to hit my  headshots and I need something a little  faster if I'm being rushed down you may  instead choose to use something a little  more flexible like an AR or SMG  the specialization is Sharpshooter  because this is the one that gives the  most benefits to a sniper build like  heat shot damage and increased armor  while in cover  I also quite like the tactician drone  just to help keep me aware of enemies  sneaking up around me  the other skill I use is the classic  reviver Hive because you know solo  player and practically no armor  and that about wraps it up pretty much  full glass Cannon so you need to utilize  cover to cover movement  as a solo player you often have to play  the sniper in a much more flexible way  and be prepared for engagements at all  ranges I wouldn't say that this was a  particularly easy playstyle but it's  certainly quite satisfying once you get  the hang of it like I said earlier there  are many ways to hit much higher numbers  but in most cases on heroic you  shouldn't need any more for one-hit  kills just land those headshots  thank you very much for watching and  I'll catch you in the next one cheers  [Music]  [Music]  foreign  [Music]

